## 6. IMPLEMENTATION NOTES — CRITICAL EDGE CASES

### Memory Management Checklist
- [ ] All geometries dispose on object pool cleanup
- [ ] All materials dispose on object pool cleanup  
- [ ] Particle pool enforces 500 hard cap via shift/push pattern
- [ ] Shockwave rings remove themselves when opacity reaches 0
- [ ] Floating text removes meshes after life expires
- [ ] Audio synth disposes oscillators on game end

### Collision Detection Edge Cases
- Player vs Enemy: AABB with 10% padding (hitbox reduction)
- Projectile vs Enemy: Circle-Circle collision (more forgiving)
- Projectile vs Player: Circle-Circle with larger hit radius for fairness
- Enemy grid bounds: Clamp movement to prevent tunneling

### Performance Guardrails
- Frame culling: Only render visible enemies in frustum
- Particle cap: Enforce 500 max active particles every frame
- Geometry merging: Merge all projectiles into single buffer geometry
- InstancedMesh: Use for starfield background (500 instances)

### VFX Priority Logic
1. Camera shake applies to camera transform directly
2. Hit-stop freezes time delta before physics updates
3. Particle manager runs after entity updates but before render
4. Shockwave rings update independently of particle system
5. Floating text renders in separate pass for performance

---

